{"packs":["ui","sector-1","sector-2","sector-3","sector-4","sector-5","sector-6"],"clips":{"Nice shot!":[0,0,4560],"Great reading!":[0,4560,4680],"You are on fire!":[0,9240,5640],"Direct hit!":[0,14880,4800],"Excellent, Cadet!":[0,19680,6000],"Now that is flying!":[0,25680,6120],"Bullseye!":[0,31800,4080],"What a pilot!":[0,35880,4680],"Tap the ship that carries the right word.":[0,40560,10800],"Miss, or wait too long, and they shoot back. Slide your ship to dodge!":[0,51360,20400],"Stuck? Tap SCAN to clear away a wrong answer.":[0,71760,15720],"Now a convoy. Zap only the animals. Let the others fly by!":[0,87480,19680],"Only zap the ships that fit.":[0,107160,8880],"Mission complete!":[0,116040,5640],"A gold medal! Perfect flying.":[0,121680,10200],"A silver medal! So close to gold.":[0,131880,10920],"A bronze medal. You made it through!":[0,142800,9840],"Emergency warp! We got out just in time. Let us try that one again.":[0,152640,22800],"Welcome to the hangar. Spend your crystals here.":[0,175440,13320],"Time for the daily patrol. Let us see what you remember!":[0,188760,16560],"Watch out! A boss ship is coming. Every right answer breaks its shield.":[0,205320,21840],"Ready, Cadet? Launch!":[0,227160,7560],"Flight school complete. Welcome to Quill Squadron!":[0,234720,15480],"Cadet! Thank the stars you are here.":[0,250200,10080],"The Garble fleet is scrambling every word in the galaxy.":[0,260280,16200],"Signs make no sense. Books are blank. Even my jokes are broken!":[0,276480,20040],"Only a pilot who knows words can stop them. That is you.":[0,296520,17280],"Climb into the Quillfire. I am Blip, and I will be your co-pilot.":[0,313800,17640],"You did it! Lord Garble is gone, and every word is back where it belongs.":[0,331440,22440],"Signs make sense. Books are full. And my jokes are funny again!":[0,353880,19080],"Thank you, Commander. The galaxy can read because of you.":[0,372960,16440],"The Garble mixed up the naming words, the action words and the describing words.":[1,0,22080],"Let's sort them out, Cadet!":[1,22080,6960],"A noun is a naming word.":[1,29040,8160],"It names a person, an animal, a place or a thing.":[1,37200,14760],"Pilot, tiger, zoo and rocket are all nouns.":[1,51960,14040],"Zap the nouns!":[1,66000,5880],"A noun names a person, an animal, a place or a thing.":[1,71880,16680],"The brave pilot fixed the engine.":[1,88560,10560],"A tiny robot carried the map.":[1,99120,9720],"The hungry tiger chased a rabbit.":[1,108840,9840],"The shiny comet crossed the sky.":[1,118680,10320],"A sleepy owl sat on the branch.":[1,129000,10680],"The clever fox found a tunnel.":[1,139680,9480],"A huge wave hit the ship.":[1,149160,8400],"The noisy rocket shook the ground.":[1,157560,10440],"A friendly alien waved at the crew.":[1,168000,11160],"The old wizard opened the gate.":[1,179160,9480],"A fluffy kitten chased the ball.":[1,188640,9600],"The captain grabbed the heavy bag.":[1,198240,9960],"The crew ate a delicious dinner.":[1,208200,9240],"The girl wore a purple helmet.":[1,217440,8880],"A cold wind rattled the windows.":[1,226320,11040],"The farmer planted yellow corn.":[1,237360,10560],"The red laser melted the rock.":[1,247920,9600],"The brave knight climbed the tower.":[1,257520,9360],"A curious monkey opened the box.":[1,266880,10920],"The tired astronaut closed the hatch.":[1,277800,11280],"The baby dropped a sticky spoon.":[1,289080,10080],"A bright star guided the sailors.":[1,299160,10440],"The teacher read a funny story.":[1,309600,9720],"The loud alarm woke the pilot.":[1,319320,9240],"A strong robot lifted the crate.":[1,328560,10800],"The doctor helped the sick puppy.":[1,339360,9360],"The gentle giant carried the children.":[1,348720,10920],"The pilot landed on a rocky moon.":[1,359640,10560],"A long tunnel led to the cave.":[1,370200,9840],"The dragon guarded a golden egg.":[1,380040,10680],"The little alien hugged the robot.":[1,390720,9600],"A slimy squid grabbed the anchor.":[1,400320,11280],"A verb is an action word.":[1,411600,8400],"It tells what someone or something does.":[1,420000,10440],"Eat, sing and build are all verbs.":[1,430440,10200],"Zap the verbs!":[1,440640,5880],"A verb is an action word. It tells what someone does.":[1,446520,16920],"An adjective is a describing word.":[1,463440,10440],"It tells what something is like.":[1,473880,8520],"Tiny, shiny and brave are all adjectives.":[1,482400,12960],"Zap the adjectives!":[1,495360,6720],"An adjective is a describing word. It tells what something is like.":[1,502080,19920],"Now find the word kinds inside a sentence.":[1,522000,13200],"Nouns name. Verbs do. Adjectives describe.":[1,535200,16560],"Read the whole sentence first. Then tap.":[1,551760,12480],"Scan the sentence!":[1,564240,6360],"A pronoun is a short word that stands in for a noun.":[1,570600,15600],"He, she, it, we and they are pronouns.":[1,586200,9480],"Instead of the pilots, you can say they.":[1,595680,10080],"Send in a stand-in!":[1,605760,6840],"A pronoun stands in for a noun: he, she, it, we, they. After the action, use him, her, it, us or them.":[1,612600,31200],"The boy found a map.":[1,643800,6960],"My grandma baked bread.":[1,650760,8160],"The rocket is fast.":[1,658920,6720],"The pilots are ready.":[1,665640,6240],"The queen smiled.":[1,671880,6480],"The king laughed.":[1,678360,5400],"The stars are bright.":[1,683760,6480],"My brother is tall.":[1,690240,6000],"The cookie is warm.":[1,696240,6720],"The engine is loud.":[1,702960,7080],"My sister can sing.":[1,710040,7200],"The robots beeped.":[1,717240,6480],"Zed and I flew home.":[1,723720,7680],"Ana and I like space.":[1,731400,7680],"Mom and Dad cheered.":[1,739080,7200],"You and I make a good team.":[1,746280,8520],"The girl and her dad waved.":[1,754800,9000],"The map and the compass are lost.":[1,763800,9720],"Blip helped the pilots.":[1,773520,7200],"I saw the comet.":[1,780720,6000],"Give the map to Ana and me.":[1,786720,7920],"We called the king.":[1,794640,5760],"I thanked my sister.":[1,800400,6960],"Blip waved at Zed and me.":[1,807360,8400],"The crew cheered for the queen.":[1,815760,8520],"Please fix the engines.":[1,824280,8160],"Listen. The Echo Belt is full of sounds, and the Garble is copying them all wrong.":[2,0,24840],"Use your ears and your eyes.":[2,24840,8520],"Rhyming words sound the same from the vowel to the end.":[2,33360,15120],"Cat rhymes with hat. They both end in at.":[2,48480,12240],"Careful! Blue rhymes with shoe, even though the letters are different.":[2,60720,18480],"Find the rhyme!":[2,79200,5400],"Rhyming words sound the same from the vowel to the end, even when the spelling is different.":[2,84600,24600],"Words have beats, called syllables.":[2,109200,10200],"Clap as you say the word. Rock, et. Two claps!":[2,119400,15720],"Zap the ship with the right number of beats.":[2,135120,11520],"Count the beats!":[2,146640,5400],"Every beat in a word has one vowel sound. Clap the word to count.":[2,152040,20400],"Vowels can be short or long.":[2,172440,9120],"A long vowel says its own name, like the A in cake.":[2,181560,16080],"A short vowel does not, like the A in cat.":[2,197640,13320],"Short or long?":[2,210960,5400],"A long vowel says its own name, like the A in cake. A short vowel does not, like the A in cat.":[2,216360,29760],"The Garble copies words and spells them wrong.":[2,246120,13320],"Only one ship has the true spelling.":[2,259440,11040],"Picture the word in your mind. Then zap the real one.":[2,270480,15720],"Find the right spelling!":[2,286200,7200],"Some words are not spelled the way they sound. Picture the word.":[2,293400,18000],"Some words sound the same but mean different things.":[2,311400,14880],"Two is a number. Too means also. To means toward.":[2,326280,14760],"Read the sentence, then pick the one that makes sense.":[2,341040,14040],"Which sound-alike?":[2,355080,5880],"Sound-alikes sound the same but have different spellings and meanings.":[2,360960,17880],"We flew to the moon.":[2,378840,6480],"The ship has two engines.":[2,385320,8280],"Can I come too?":[2,393600,5640],"I can see a comet!":[2,399240,6720],"The whale swam in the sea.":[2,405960,8040],"I know the answer!":[2,414000,6000],"There is no air in space.":[2,420000,8880],"The sun is a very hot star.":[2,428880,9600],"The king hugged his son.":[2,438480,7080],"This map is for you.":[2,445560,6480],"A dog has four legs.":[2,452040,8640],"A bee buzzed past my helmet.":[2,460680,10080],"I want to be a pilot.":[2,470760,6600],"We won the race!":[2,477360,5400],"I have one little robot.":[2,482760,7920],"Mars looks red in the sky.":[2,490680,9000],"Neptune looks blue.":[2,499680,7200],"Come over here!":[2,506880,4800],"The crew ate dinner at six.":[2,511680,8880],"A spider has eight legs.":[2,520560,9000],"I want to buy a new helmet.":[2,529560,7800],"The comet flew right by us.":[2,537360,8640],"I read that book last week.":[2,546000,8760],"The wind blew the flag away.":[2,554760,9480],"Did you hear that beep?":[2,564240,6480],"We got a new ship.":[2,570720,6120],"I knew you could do it!":[2,576840,6240],"Let's meet at the launch pad.":[2,583080,8760],"The lion ate the meat.":[2,591840,6840],"She rode her bike to school.":[2,598680,8640],"The road was long and bumpy.":[2,607320,9720],"The comet has a long tail.":[2,617040,9240],"Grandpa told a tall tale.":[2,626280,9720],"We launch next week.":[2,636000,7200],"The signal is too weak.":[2,643200,7680],"Turn right at the red star.":[2,650880,8400],"Please write your name here.":[2,659280,7320],"She picked a yellow flower.":[2,666600,8280],"Bread is made from flour.":[2,674880,8400],"I ate the whole pizza!":[2,683280,6960],"The mouse hid in a hole.":[2,690240,7320],"The pilots put on their helmets.":[2,697560,9120],"Park the ship over there.":[2,706680,7560],"They're ready to launch.":[2,714240,6480],"Is this your helmet?":[2,720720,6240],"You're a great pilot!":[2,726960,6000],"The robot lost its arm.":[2,732960,8640],"It's time to go!":[2,741600,5640],"The ball went through the window.":[2,747240,8280],"He threw the ball to me.":[2,755520,7080],"May I have a piece of pie?":[2,762600,7920],"Step on the brake to stop.":[2,770520,7920],"Do not break the window!":[2,778440,7080],"Which ship is yours?":[2,785520,6720],"I wear a helmet in space.":[2,792240,8640],"Where is my helmet?":[2,800880,6000],"The table is made of wood.":[2,806880,8520],"Would you like a ride?":[2,815400,6480],"Please wait for me!":[2,821880,6000],"The plane landed on the runway.":[2,827880,9600],"Put the words in ABC order.":[2,837480,9720],"Look at the first letter of each word.":[2,847200,10080],"If the first letters match, look at the second letters.":[2,857280,14640],"Zap in ABC order!":[2,871920,8040],"Look at the first letters. If they match, look at the next letters.":[2,879960,17760],"These stars shine with meaning. The Garble wants to switch every word with its opposite.":[3,0,24600],"Know what the words mean, and you win.":[3,24600,9600],"Synonyms are words with the same meaning.":[3,34200,11280],"Big and large are synonyms.":[3,45480,8520],"Watch out. The Garble hides an opposite in every wave.":[3,54000,16920],"Find the twin!":[3,70920,5520],"Synonyms are words that mean the same, or almost the same.":[3,76440,17640],"Antonyms are opposites.":[3,94080,7680],"Hot and cold are antonyms. So are up and down.":[3,101760,13920],"This time, do not zap the twin. Zap the opposite!":[3,115680,15840],"Find the opposite!":[3,131520,6000],"Antonyms are opposites, like hot and cold.":[3,137520,13200],"Sometimes you meet a word you do not know.":[3,150720,10800],"Do not panic. The other words in the sentence are clues.":[3,161520,16440],"Read the whole sentence. Then choose what the glowing word means.":[3,177960,18840],"Catch the clue!":[3,196800,5160],"When you meet a new word, the words around it are clues to what it means.":[3,201960,18360],"I was so famished that I ate three sandwiches.":[3,220320,13920],"The enormous ship was bigger than a whale.":[3,234240,11880],"The swift rocket zoomed past in one second.":[3,246120,14040],"The ancient map was made a thousand years ago.":[3,260160,13920],"She was furious and stomped her feet.":[3,274080,10800],"He was delighted with the gift and could not stop smiling.":[3,284880,15840],"My socks were drenched after I stepped in the puddle.":[3,300720,14040],"The puppy was filthy after rolling in the mud.":[3,314760,13440],"The frigid wind turned my nose to ice.":[3,328200,12240],"It was scorching outside, so we stayed in the cool pool.":[3,340440,15840],"We felt drowsy after lunch and started to yawn.":[3,356280,14520],"The knight was courageous and faced the dragon alone.":[3,370800,14040],"Be careful! That glass vase is fragile and breaks easily.":[3,384840,19440],"After the long hike, the weary pilot fell asleep fast.":[3,404280,16800],"The alien's hat was peculiar. I had never seen one like it!":[3,421080,18840],"The timid kitten hid under the bed when guests came.":[3,439920,14400],"The magician made the coin vanish. It was gone!":[3,454320,14280],"The stars glimmer like tiny lights in the dark sky.":[3,468600,15480],"Be cautious on the icy steps so you do not slip.":[3,484080,14640],"Dad will mend my torn jacket with a needle and thread.":[3,498720,15000],"A strong odor came from the old cheese. Yuck!":[3,513720,15720],"The eagle can soar high above the clouds.":[3,529440,12480],"The sturdy bridge held ten heavy trucks.":[3,541920,11880],"My hands tremble when I am nervous.":[3,553800,10800],"The ship will depart at noon, so say goodbye before then.":[3,564600,16920],"She gave a brief talk. It lasted only one minute.":[3,581520,15600],"The room was vacant. No one was inside.":[3,597120,12600],"The crowd began to applaud by clapping loudly.":[3,609720,14040],"The steps were jagged, with sharp, pointy edges.":[3,623760,14160],"The nimble monkey leaped easily from branch to branch.":[3,637920,15840],"Let me ponder your question for a minute before I answer.":[3,653760,14880],"We climbed to the summit and looked down from the top.":[3,668640,12960],"The doctor will examine your ear with a little light.":[3,681600,13800],"The clumsy robot kept bumping into walls.":[3,695400,13920],"Blue diamonds are rare. Almost no one has seen one.":[3,709320,17040],"The squirrels gather nuts and pile them up for winter.":[3,726360,14760],"The fog was so dense that we could not see the road.":[3,741120,14760],"The trail was hazardous, with falling rocks everywhere.":[3,755880,15600],"A gust of wind blew my hat right off.":[3,771480,12720],"The scientist will observe the birds with her telescope.":[3,784200,15600],"Some words are stronger than others.":[3,799800,9960],"Warm is a little. Hot is more. Scorching is the most.":[3,809760,16680],"Check the banner. It tells you which end of the ladder to find.":[3,826440,17760],"Rank the words!":[3,844200,5640],"Some words mean almost the same, but one is stronger: warm, hot, scorching.":[3,849840,23520],"Some words are double agents. They have two meanings.":[3,873360,14520],"A bat is a flying animal. A bat is also a stick for hitting a ball.":[3,887880,20880],"Read both clues. One word fits them both.":[3,908760,13440],"Unmask the double agent!":[3,922200,8520],"One word can have two different meanings, like bat.":[3,930720,13440],"Which word can mean both: a flying animal, and a stick for hitting a ball?":[3,944160,21480],"Which word can mean both: the sound a dog makes, and the skin of a tree?":[3,965640,21120],"Which word can mean both: a buzzing bug, and what a rocket can do?":[3,986760,19800],"Which word can mean both: a quacking bird, and to drop down fast and hide?":[3,1006560,22920],"Which word can mean both: a light in the night sky, and a famous actor?":[3,1029480,21120],"Which word can mean both: a stone, and to move back and forth?":[3,1050600,18480],"Which word can mean both: not heavy, and what a lamp gives?":[3,1069080,16800],"Which word can mean both: a metal container, and to be able to?":[3,1085880,19680],"Which word can mean both: a small animal, and a computer tool you click?":[3,1105560,22080],"Which word can mean both: a season, and to tumble down?":[3,1127640,17280],"Which word can mean both: not warm, and a sickness with sneezing?":[3,1144920,19560],"Which word can mean both: a piece of mail, and one part of the alphabet?":[3,1164480,21840],"Which word can mean both: jewelry for your finger, and the sound of a bell?":[3,1186320,20400],"Which word can mean both: water rolling onto the beach, and to move your hand to say hi?":[3,1206720,25800],"Which word can mean both: a clock on your wrist, and to look at something?":[3,1232520,20520],"Which word can mean both: the opposite of left, and correct?":[3,1253040,17400],"Which word can mean both: a tool that cuts wood, and looked at something before?":[3,1270440,22320],"Which word can mean both: an elephant's nose, and the back of a car?":[3,1292760,20400],"Which word can mean both: a sea animal, and to close something tight?":[3,1313160,20640],"Which word can mean both: a writing tool, and a fenced place for pigs?":[3,1333800,21000],"Which word can mean both: a season, and a metal coil that bounces?":[3,1354800,21720],"Which word can mean both: a place to play outside, and to stop a car in a spot?":[3,1376520,24120],"Which word can mean both: fruit spread for toast, and cars stuck on the road?":[3,1400640,22560],"Which word can mean both: a dish for soup, and to roll a ball at pins?":[3,1423200,21360],"Which word can mean both: a baseball thrower, and a jug for pouring?":[3,1444560,20520],"Which word can mean both: the inside of your hand, and a tree with coconuts?":[3,1465080,22560],"Which word can mean both: a student, and the dark center of your eye?":[3,1487640,20520],"Which word can mean both: the side of a river, and a place that keeps money?":[3,1508160,21000],"Which word can mean both: a very short bit of time, and right after first?":[3,1529160,22080],"Which word can mean both: the hard tip of your finger, and a metal pin you hammer?":[3,1551240,23040],"Which word can mean both: a stick you strike to make fire, and a contest between two teams?":[3,1574280,28080],"Which word can mean both: nice and caring, and a type of something?":[3,1602360,20400],"Words are built from parts here. The Garble has been snapping them to pieces.":[4,0,22200],"Let's put them back together.":[4,22200,7680],"Two small words can join to make a new word.":[4,29880,12120],"Rain plus bow makes rainbow.":[4,42000,9240],"Find the piece that makes a real word.":[4,51240,10320],"Fuse the words!":[4,61560,5880],"A compound word is two smaller words joined into one.":[4,67440,17040],"A prefix is a word part that goes on the front.":[4,84480,13200],"Un means not. Unhappy means not happy.":[4,97680,13920],"Re means again. Replay means play again.":[4,111600,12840],"Power up with a prefix!":[4,124440,7080],"A prefix goes on the front of a word and changes its meaning. Un means not. Re means again.":[4,131520,29040],"A suffix is a word part that goes on the end.":[4,160560,13320],"Ful means full of. Hopeful means full of hope.":[4,173880,14040],"Less means without. Fearless means without fear.":[4,187920,14400],"Check the ending!":[4,202320,5640],"A suffix goes on the end of a word. Ful means full of. Less means without.":[4,207960,23760],"A rocket is blank than a bike.":[4,231720,9480],"Jupiter is the blank of the eight planets.":[4,241200,12240],"The moon is blank than the sun.":[4,253440,9600],"That was the blank joke ever!":[4,263040,8400],"My dog is blank than my cat.":[4,271440,9840],"This is the blank day of the year.":[4,281280,9840],"A turtle is blank than a rabbit.":[4,291120,10080],"She is the blank runner of all.":[4,301200,9360],"A feather is blank than a rock.":[4,310560,9600],"This is the blank mountain on Earth.":[4,320160,10680],"Ice is blank than water.":[4,330840,8400],"He is the blank pilot of all.":[4,339240,9120],"Plural means more than one.":[4,348360,8280],"Most words just add an S, like one star, two stars.":[4,356640,16440],"Some add E S, like one fox, two foxes. And some change completely, like one mouse, two mice.":[4,373080,30840],"Make it more than one!":[4,403920,6480],"Most words just add an S. Words that end in S, X, C H or S H add E S. A consonant and Y changes to I E S. Some F words change to V E S. A few words change completely.":[4,410400,62760],"Verbs change when something already happened.":[4,473160,11400],"Most add E D, like jump and jumped.":[4,484560,11040],"Some are rebels. Today I run. Yesterday I ran.":[4,495600,15720],"Jump to yesterday!":[4,511320,6600],"Most verbs add E D for the past. Some double a letter or change Y to I first. Some change completely, like run and ran.":[4,517920,39840],"A contraction squeezes two words into one.":[4,557760,13200],"Do not becomes don't.":[4,570960,6720],"The apostrophe stands where letters were taken out.":[4,577680,14040],"Squeeze the words!":[4,591720,6000],"A contraction squeezes two words into one. An apostrophe takes the place of the missing letters.":[4,597720,28800],"Sentence Station sends every message in the galaxy. The Garble pulled out all the marks and capitals.":[5,0,29400],"Time to fix the mail.":[5,29400,7200],"A complete sentence is a whole thought.":[5,36600,10560],"It tells who or what. And it tells what they do.":[5,47160,14400],"The rocket landed. That is complete. The shiny rocket. That is only a piece.":[5,61560,23640],"Find the whole sentence!":[5,85200,7200],"A complete sentence tells who or what, and what they do or are.":[5,92400,17160],"Every sentence needs an end mark.":[5,109560,10080],"Telling sentences get a period. Asking sentences get a question mark.":[5,119640,22560],"Shouts and strong feelings get an exclamation point!":[5,142200,15120],"Pick the end mark!":[5,157320,6360],"A telling sentence ends with a period, an asking sentence with a question mark, and a shout with an exclamation point.":[5,163680,35160],"Some words need a capital letter.":[5,198840,9720],"The first word of a sentence. Names of people and places. Days and months. And the word \"I\".":[5,208560,29760],"Tap every word that needs one.":[5,238320,9480],"Give them capitals!":[5,247800,6000],"The first word, names of people and places, days, months and the word \"I\" all start with a capital.":[5,253800,30720],"The verb has to match who is doing it.":[5,284520,10560],"One pilot is ready. Two pilots are ready.":[5,295080,13440],"Say the sentence in your head. Pick the one that sounds right.":[5,308520,16800],"Make them match!":[5,325320,5280],"The verb has to match who is doing it: one pilot is, two pilots are.":[5,330600,21000],"The pilots blank ready.":[5,351600,7680],"The rocket blank fast.":[5,359280,7920],"I blank a pilot.":[5,367200,6000],"We blank in space.":[5,373200,7080],"She blank my sister.":[5,380280,7320],"The stars blank bright.":[5,387600,7800],"Blip blank a robot.":[5,395400,7200],"They blank late.":[5,402600,5760],"You blank brave.":[5,408360,6240],"The moon blank full.":[5,414600,6960],"She blank to the moon.":[5,421560,6960],"The dogs blank loudly.":[5,428520,8400],"He blank the ship.":[5,436920,6120],"Birds blank south.":[5,443040,7200],"My sister blank fast.":[5,450240,8040],"The captain blank at noon.":[5,458280,8040],"The boys blank the map.":[5,466320,7920],"A comet blank across the sky.":[5,474240,10200],"We blank our helmets.":[5,484440,7200],"It blank a lot here.":[5,491640,6480],"The robots blank the floor.":[5,498120,9000],"Ana blank the stars.":[5,507120,7800],"The ship blank late yesterday.":[5,514920,9600],"The ships blank late yesterday.":[5,524520,10080],"We blank at the base last night.":[5,534600,9600],"I blank sleepy last night.":[5,544200,8760],"She blank a new helmet.":[5,552960,7320],"They blank two robots.":[5,560280,8040],"He blank not like peas.":[5,568320,7920],"We blank not have a map.":[5,576240,7440],"The pilot and the crew blank ready.":[5,583680,9840],"One of the engines blank broken.":[5,593520,9840],"Everyone blank here.":[5,603360,6960],"There blank three moons.":[5,610320,7440],"There blank one sun.":[5,617760,6720],"Little marks do big jobs.":[5,624480,8640],"Commas split up a list. An apostrophe shows who owns something.":[5,633120,19440],"Quotation marks go around the words someone says.":[5,652560,14640],"Find the one marked right!":[5,667200,7800],"Commas split up a list. An apostrophe shows who owns something. Quotation marks hold the words someone says.":[5,675000,34320],"Joining words link two ideas.":[5,709320,10080],"And adds more. But shows a surprise. Or gives a choice.":[5,719400,16200],"So tells what happened next. Because tells why.":[5,735600,13800],"Link the ideas!":[5,749400,6360],"And adds. But shows a change. Or gives a choice. So tells what happened next. Because tells why.":[5,755760,29760],"I was tired, blank I went to bed.":[5,785520,10440],"I brought a map blank a compass.":[5,795960,9360],"I wanted to fly, blank my ship was broken.":[5,805320,13440],"We can walk, blank we can take the rover.":[5,818760,11520],"We stayed inside blank it was raining.":[5,830280,11520],"It was raining, blank we stayed inside.":[5,841800,12240],"I like apples, blank I do not like pears.":[5,854040,13080],"Do you want milk blank juice?":[5,867120,8640],"She put on her helmet blank her boots.":[5,875760,10680],"The alarm rang, blank nobody woke up.":[5,886440,12720],"He studied hard, blank he passed the test.":[5,899160,12720],"I cannot see blank it is too dark.":[5,911880,10680],"Hurry up, blank we will miss the launch!":[5,922560,10680],"The ship is old, blank it still flies fast.":[5,933240,14040],"Ana laughed blank the joke was funny.":[5,947280,11280],"We were hungry, blank we made tacos.":[5,958560,11640],"The puppy is small, blank it is very loud.":[5,970200,13320],"Zed missed the bus blank he woke up late.":[5,983520,11880],"The door was locked, blank we used the window.":[5,995400,13080],"I wanted to stay up, blank I was too sleepy.":[5,1008480,12600],"Wear a coat, blank you will be cold.":[5,1021080,10320],"The engine is fixed, blank we can leave now.":[5,1031400,13320],"She smiled blank she won the race.":[5,1044720,10560],"I looked everywhere, blank I could not find it.":[5,1055280,12480],"The Garble shuffled the words.":[5,1067760,8640],"Zap them in order to build the sentence.":[5,1076400,10680],"Clue: start with the capital letter. Finish with the end mark.":[5,1087080,17400],"Build the sentence!":[5,1104480,6120],"A sentence starts with a capital letter and stops at the end mark.":[5,1110600,18000],"This is it. The heart of the Garble fleet hides in the Story Galaxy.":[6,0,20880],"Read carefully. Every story holds the clues you need.":[6,20880,15840],"Time to read a message from the fleet.":[6,36720,9720],"Read it all the way through. No rush.":[6,46440,10440],"Then answer the question. You can look back any time.":[6,56880,15000],"Read the log!":[6,71880,4920],"The main idea is what the whole passage is mostly about. Details are the small facts inside it.":[6,76800,29640],"The Leaky Ship":[6,106440,5400],"Zed heard a hiss. Air was leaking from the ship! First, Zed put on his helmet. Next, he found the tiny hole. Then he covered it with sticky tape. At last, the hissing stopped. Zed smiled and gave a thumbs-up.":[6,111840,69480],"Moon Dust":[6,181320,5040],"The moon is covered in gray dust. There is no wind or rain on the moon. That means footprints stay for a very long time. The boot prints from the first astronauts are still there today!":[6,186360,60600],"Blip's Birthday":[6,246960,5640],"It was Blip's birthday. The crew hid behind the crates. When Blip rolled in, everyone jumped out and yelled, \"Surprise!\" Blip's lights flashed pink. He spun in circles and beeped a happy song.":[6,252600,65280],"The Thirsty Plant":[6,317880,6240],"Ana planted a seed in a cup on the ship. It grew into a little plant. Then she forgot to water it for a week. The plant drooped and turned yellow. Ana gave it water and put it by the window. Two days later, it stood tall and green again.":[6,324120,76200],"The Amazing Octopus":[6,400320,8160],"An octopus has eight arms and three hearts. It can squeeze through a tiny hole because it has no bones. When danger is near, it squirts dark ink and zooms away.":[6,408480,53040],"The Lost Map":[6,461520,5640],"Captain Mira could not find her star map. She looked under her seat. She looked in the cargo room. At last, she asked Blip. Blip pointed at her hand. She had been holding the map the whole time!":[6,467160,60720],"Day and Night":[6,527880,4800],"Earth spins like a top. It takes one day to spin all the way around. When your side of Earth faces the sun, you have daytime. When your side turns away from the sun, it is night.":[6,532680,57840],"Garble Trouble":[6,590520,5520],"A Garbler sneaked into the kitchen. It scrambled every label. The salt jar said SUGAR. The sugar jar said SALT. At breakfast, Zed put two spoons of \"sugar\" on his cereal. He took one bite and made a terrible face.":[6,596040,73080],"Tiny Flier":[6,669120,5280],"A hummingbird is tiny, but it is a mighty flier. Its wings beat so fast that they hum. It can hover in one spot like a helicopter. It can even fly backward! It drinks sweet nectar from flowers to get energy.":[6,674400,70200],"The Rover Race":[6,744600,6000],"Leo and Ana raced their rovers across the red sand. Leo zoomed ahead and waved at the crowd. He did not see the big rock. Crunch! His rover stopped. Ana drove slowly and steadily past him and won.":[6,750600,68040],"Make a Crater":[6,818640,4680],"You can make moon craters at home. First, fill a pan with flour. Next, sprinkle cocoa powder on top. Then drop a marble into the pan. Last, lift the marble out and look at your crater!":[6,823320,61440],"The Little Rover":[6,884760,5280],"The rover Spark was built to explore a cold, dusty planet. Its mission was to last ninety days. But Spark kept rolling for many years! It climbed hills, took pictures, and sent them home. The scientists cheered each time.":[6,890040,75000],"Sleepy Bears":[6,965040,5880],"In fall, bears eat as much as they can. They grow very fat. When winter comes, food is hard to find. So bears curl up in a den and sleep for months. Their fat keeps them alive until spring.":[6,970920,64560],"The Trade":[6,1035480,4200],"Zed wanted Ana's glowing rock. Ana wanted Zed's toy comet. \"Let's trade,\" said Zed. They swapped. That night, Zed's rock glowed by his bed, and Ana's comet spun on her shelf. Both friends fell asleep smiling.":[6,1039680,74160],"Shooting Stars":[6,1113840,6120],"A shooting star is not really a star. It is a small rock from space. When it falls into the air around Earth, it gets so hot that it glows. We call that bright streak a meteor.":[6,1119960,55920],"The Quiet Planet":[6,1175880,6000],"The crew landed on a quiet green planet. Tiny footprints led from the ship to a cave. Inside, they found a nest made of soft moss. Three blue eggs sat in the nest, still warm.":[6,1181880,63000],"What is this story mostly about?":[6,1244880,9480],"What covers the moon?":[6,1254360,6840],"What is this mostly about?":[6,1261200,7920],"Where did the crew hide?":[6,1269120,6480],"What color was the plant at the end?":[6,1275600,9960],"How many hearts does an octopus have?":[6,1285560,10680],"Who showed Mira where the map was?":[6,1296240,9360],"How long does one full spin take?":[6,1305600,10440],"What did the salt jar say?":[6,1316040,7920],"What makes the humming sound?":[6,1323960,7920],"What does a hummingbird drink?":[6,1331880,8400],"Where did they race?":[6,1340280,5760],"What do you drop into the pan?":[6,1346040,8280],"How long was the mission supposed to last?":[6,1354320,12000],"What kind of planet did Spark explore?":[6,1366320,11520],"What keeps bears alive in winter?":[6,1377840,9480],"What did Ana get in the trade?":[6,1387320,8040],"What is a shooting star really?":[6,1395360,8640],"What do we call the bright streak?":[6,1404000,8280],"What was the nest made of?":[6,1412280,7200],"How many eggs were in the nest?":[6,1419480,8400],"Stories happen in order.":[6,1427880,7440],"Look for clue words. First. Next. Then. Last.":[6,1435320,17400],"Read carefully, then tell what happened when.":[6,1452720,11760],"Track the order!":[6,1464480,5400],"Words like first, next, then and last tell you the order things happen.":[6,1469880,20280],"What did Zed do first?":[6,1490160,7080],"What happened right after Blip rolled in?":[6,1497240,10920],"What did Ana do after the plant turned yellow?":[6,1508160,12360],"Where did Mira look first?":[6,1520520,7320],"What happened before breakfast?":[6,1527840,9000],"What happened after Leo's rover stopped?":[6,1536840,11640],"What do you do right after filling the pan with flour?":[6,1548480,13920],"What is the last step?":[6,1562400,6720],"What do bears do when winter comes?":[6,1569120,10560],"What happened that night?":[6,1579680,6480],"Things happen for a reason.":[6,1586160,7560],"The reason is the cause. What happens is the effect.":[6,1593720,15360],"Ask yourself: why did that happen?":[6,1609080,9840],"Find out why!":[6,1618920,5520],"A cause is why something happens. An effect is what happens.":[6,1624440,16920],"Why did Zed hear a hiss?":[6,1641360,6960],"Why do footprints stay on the moon?":[6,1648320,10200],"Why did the crew hide?":[6,1658520,6480],"Why did the plant droop?":[6,1665000,7080],"Why can an octopus fit through a tiny hole?":[6,1672080,12360],"Why do we have night?":[6,1684440,5760],"Why were the labels wrong?":[6,1690200,7080],"Why did Leo's rover stop?":[6,1697280,8280],"Why do bears eat so much in fall?":[6,1705560,10200],"Why did they trade?":[6,1715760,6120],"Why does the falling rock glow?":[6,1721880,9000],"Some answers are not written in the passage.":[6,1730880,11640],"Be a detective. Put the clues together.":[6,1742520,11400],"Clues plus what you already know make a smart guess.":[6,1753920,13800],"Be a detective!":[6,1767720,5160],"An inference is a smart guess. Use clues from the passage and what you already know.":[6,1772880,24600],"How did Zed feel at the end?":[6,1797480,8400],"What happens to a footprint on a windy beach?":[6,1805880,12360],"How did Blip feel?":[6,1818240,6240],"What does this story show about plants?":[6,1824480,10560],"Why does an octopus squirt ink?":[6,1835040,9240],"How did Mira most likely feel at the end?":[6,1844280,11760],"When it is night for you, what is it on the other side of Earth?":[6,1856040,15720],"Why did Zed make a terrible face?":[6,1871760,10320],"Why does a hummingbird need so much energy?":[6,1882080,12120],"What lesson does this story teach?":[6,1894200,9960],"What is the marble pretending to be?":[6,1904160,9840],"Why did the scientists cheer?":[6,1914000,8520],"How did both friends feel about the trade?":[6,1922520,11160],"What do the warm eggs tell you?":[6,1933680,8520],"Who most likely made the tiny footprints?":[6,1942200,11520],"A fact is something you can check and prove.":[6,1953720,11760],"An opinion is what someone thinks or feels.":[6,1965480,12960],"Words like best, worst, fun and boring are opinion clues.":[6,1978440,19200],"Fact or opinion?":[6,1997640,6480],"A fact can be proven true. An opinion is what someone thinks or feels.":[6,2004120,22560],"The sun is a star.":[6,2026680,6720],"A week has seven days.":[6,2033400,8640],"Spiders have eight legs.":[6,2042040,8520],"Earth has one moon.":[6,2050560,7200],"Ice is frozen water.":[6,2057760,7920],"A triangle has three sides.":[6,2065680,10320],"Fish live in water.":[6,2076000,6720],"Mars is a planet.":[6,2082720,6600],"Bees make honey.":[6,2089320,5760],"A year has twelve months.":[6,2095080,8280],"Owls can fly.":[6,2103360,6480],"The moon goes around Earth.":[6,2109840,8160],"Dogs have four legs.":[6,2118000,8040],"Cows give milk.":[6,2126040,6120],"Trees have roots.":[6,2132160,6240],"Saturn has rings.":[6,2138400,7200],"A dime is worth ten cents.":[6,2145600,9120],"Birds lay eggs.":[6,2154720,6960],"Mars is the most exciting planet.":[6,2161680,11280],"Pizza is the best dinner.":[6,2172960,7680],"Dogs are better than cats.":[6,2180640,8400],"Winter is too long.":[6,2189040,7080],"Blue is the prettiest color.":[6,2196120,8520],"Math is more fun than art.":[6,2204640,9000],"Robots are scary.":[6,2213640,6600],"Everyone should have a pet.":[6,2220240,7440],"Space movies are boring.":[6,2227680,8520],"Summer is the best season.":[6,2236200,8640],"Broccoli tastes yucky.":[6,2244840,8160],"Saturn is the most beautiful planet.":[6,2253000,11520],"Mondays are the worst.":[6,2264520,7320],"That was the funniest joke ever.":[6,2271840,9360],"Soccer is easy.":[6,2281200,6360],"Rain is annoying.":[6,2287560,6480],"Night is nicer than day.":[6,2294040,8880],"Ice cream is the best treat.":[6,2302920,9000],"Some sayings do not mean what the words say.":[6,2311920,12000],"Raining cats and dogs just means raining very hard.":[6,2323920,15840],"Think about what the speaker really means.":[6,2339760,10680],"Crack the saying!":[6,2350440,5640],"Some sayings do not mean exactly what the words say.":[6,2356080,14880],"The baby was as quiet as a mouse.":[6,2370960,10560],"My backpack is as light as a feather.":[6,2381520,10920],"He ran as fast as lightning.":[6,2392440,9240],"She is as brave as a lion.":[6,2401680,9120],"The floor was as cold as ice.":[6,2410800,9360],"He is as busy as a bee.":[6,2420160,8280],"The pillow was as soft as a cloud.":[6,2428440,10320],"I slept like a log.":[6,2438760,7080],"He eats like a bird.":[6,2445840,6720],"The news spread like wildfire.":[6,2452560,10080],"It is raining cats and dogs.":[6,2462640,9960],"That test was a piece of cake.":[6,2472600,9240],"I am feeling under the weather.":[6,2481840,7800],"Time to hit the hay.":[6,2489640,6600],"I have butterflies in my stomach.":[6,2496240,9840],"Hold your horses!":[6,2506080,6360],"I am all ears.":[6,2512440,5640],"She let the cat out of the bag.":[6,2518080,8640],"That ride was out of this world!":[6,2526720,9480],"He is in hot water.":[6,2536200,6600],"Zip your lips.":[6,2542800,5640],"Can you lend me a hand?":[6,2548440,6720],"Hang in there!":[6,2555160,5040],"It happens once in a blue moon.":[6,2560200,9600],"She was over the moon.":[6,2569800,6360],"Reach for the stars.":[6,2576160,6960],"He got cold feet.":[6,2583120,6600],"It cost an arm and a leg.":[6,2589720,8880],"Break a leg!":[6,2598600,4920],"I am on cloud nine.":[6,2603520,7560],"Do not spill the beans.":[6,2611080,7440],"We see eye to eye.":[6,2618520,6360],"He has a heart of gold.":[6,2624880,7200],"Time flies when you are having fun.":[6,2632080,10680],"I felt like a fish out of water.":[6,2642760,9120]}}